{
  "abstract": "Let F(n) be the maximal length of a 2-increasing sequence of triples in {1..n}^3, where a triple is 2-less than another if it is smaller in at least two coordinates. Gowers and Long show that F(n) ≥ n^{3/2} when n is a perfect square (arXiv:1609.08688, Proposition 1.4). The package proves (√n)^3 ≤ F(n) for every perfect square n.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Wentao Li"
    }
  ],
